<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · site</p><h1 class="enc-title">Calleva Atrebatum</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Silchester</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Calleva Atrebatum was an <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/iron-age">Iron Age</a> and Roman town at Silchester in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hampshire">Hampshire</a>, in southern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/england">England</a>. It began as an oppidum of the Atrebates in the late 1st century BCE and became the tribe's civitas capital after the Roman conquest. Abandoned in the early <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/middle-ages">Middle Ages</a> and never built over, it is one of the most fully excavated Roman towns in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/britain">Britain</a>, and its walls still stand.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/calleva-atrebatum.jpg" alt="Calleva Atrebatum" width="320" height="286" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Orig: Encyclopaedia Britannica Vector work: Hogweard · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Calleva_Atrebatum_plan.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
